-- `RDX0116` — doc 18 §4's `(|> name)` method reference, retired by plan 57.
--
-- The replacement is a bare `.name`, which lowers to the same
-- `|__rdx_1| __rdx_1.name()`, so the construct survives and only the spelling
-- goes. Plan 65's rule says which row removes it: whoever builds the
-- replacement.
--
-- `(.name)` is **not** refused, and the second line is the fixture for that:
-- it is the field selector, and a `)` immediately after the name is the whole
-- discriminator. A fixture asserting only the refusal would stay green if the
-- selector were refused too.

main : ()
main =
  method_ref = (|> len)
  selector = (.name)
  print 1
  ()
